<title>DEMOCRATIC REPUBLIC OF CONGO: New Congo consumer prices said down 10 pct in June.</title>
<headline>New Congo consumer prices said down 10 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>KINSHASA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer prices in the Democratic Republic of the Congo fell 10.0 percent in June compared with May, cutting the year-on-year inflation rate to 272 percent from 352 percent, according to data compiled by the U.S. embassy in Kinshasa.</p>
<p>					   June		May</p>
<p>	  Change on month	    -10.0 pct	 -20.1 pct</p>
<p>	  Change on year	     +272.0 pct	+352.0 pct</p>
<p>	  Index (base 1989 = 100)  108,112	    120,127</p>
<p>Year-on-year inflation in April stood at 560 percent, just before ex-Zaire dictator Mobutu Sese Seko was ousted from power.</p>
<p>Inflation in 1996 was 741 percent, compared to 382 percent in 1995 and 6,030 percent in 1994.</p>
<p>-- Abidjan newsroom, +225 21 90 90</p>
